Cluster & Resource Exploration
- kubectl get nodes – List all nodes in the cluster
- kubectl get pods – List all pods in the current namespace
- kubectl get services – List all services
- kubectl get deployments – List all deployments
- kubectl get all – Show all common resources (pods, services, deployments, etc.)

---

📦 Creating & Managing Resources
- kubectl create -f <filename>.yaml – Create resources from a YAML file
- kubectl apply -f <filename>.yaml – Apply changes from a YAML file (create or update)
- kubectl delete -f <filename>.yaml – Delete resources defined in a YAML file
- kubectl delete pod <pod-name> – Delete a specific pod

---

🔍 Inspecting & Debugging
- kubectl describe pod <pod-name> – Detailed info about a pod
- kubectl logs <pod-name> – View logs of a pod
- kubectl exec -it <pod-name> -- /bin/bash – Access a pod’s shell interactively

---

📈 Scaling & Updating
- kubectl scale deployment <deployment-name> --replicas=3 – Scale a deployment
- kubectl rollout status deployment/<deployment-name> – Check rollout status
- kubectl rollout undo deployment/<deployment-name> – Roll back to previous version

---

🧪 Useful Flags
- -n <namespace> – Specify a namespace
- -o wide – Get extended output (e.g., node IPs)
- --all-namespaces – View resources across all namespaces
